# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT a .tf file on purpose -- see the warning below.
#
# GITOPS.md lists "MinIO CORS handled by a Cloudflare Transform Rule" as a
# clickops gap. It is deliberately NOT scaffolded here, for two reasons.
#
# 1. The rule cannot be read without an API token, so anything written now would
#    be a guess. Applying a guessed Transform Rule would overwrite the real one
#    with something untested -- strictly worse than leaving it in the dashboard.
#    Transcribe the live rule first, then encode it.
#
# 2. It may not be needed at all. sunfire/HOMELAB.md records: "Only
#    browser-direct access needs this; server-side callers don't." The Worker is
#    the only client of MinIO -- end users never touch the origin
#    (sunfire/homelab/README.md, "the access model") -- so if nothing fetches
#    bucket objects directly from a browser, this rule is vestigial and the
#    right move is to DELETE it rather than codify it.
#
# Decide which of those it is before writing a resource. The question to answer:
# does any browser fetch minio-api.sunosrs.cc directly, or does every byte go
# through the Worker?
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
